WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.251 --> 00:00:03.670
SPEAKER: Duty is sacrifice.

2
00:00:05.213 --> 00:00:07.173
It eclipses all things.

3
00:00:07.882 --> 00:00:09.092
even blood.

4
00:00:10.927 --> 00:00:12.047
In the making of season one.

5
00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:14.014
we knew half that
season is a prologue

6
00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:16.306
and half of it is the
first act of this war.

7
00:00:16.433 --> 00:00:18.685
To have season one
land the way it did.

8
00:00:18.768 --> 00:00:20.478
with a rabid audience.

9
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.148
fans of George and his
books the way I am.

10
00:00:23.231 --> 00:00:24.431
We were excited to get into it

11
00:00:24.482 --> 00:00:27.360
because this is the
juicy part of the drama.

12
00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.529
♪ (SOMBER MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

13
00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:35.577
SPEAKER: The North owes a great
duty to the Seven Kingdoms.

14
00:00:36.077 --> 00:00:38.079
one older than any oath.

15
00:00:38.621 --> 00:00:41.124
Winterfell is the one place.
the one corner of this world

16
00:00:41.166 --> 00:00:43.668
where news of Luke's
death has not yet reached.

17
00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:48.423
and it is this hearkening
back to a simpler time.

18
00:00:48.506 --> 00:00:51.634
I wanted to go to a place
where we could experience that.

19
00:00:51.676 --> 00:00:52.676
if only briefly.

20
00:00:52.844 --> 00:00:55.388
and the North just felt
completely the right way to go.

21
00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.224
Ryan. when we did speak. it
really. really helped me out

22
00:00:58.308 --> 00:01:00.518
because we would
have conversations

23
00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.396
about how important
these negotiations are

24
00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:04.272
for Team Black

25
00:01:04.438 --> 00:01:07.025
and the difference
it makes in the war.

26
00:01:07.108 --> 00:01:10.028
War is coming to the whole
of the realm. My Lord.

27
00:01:10.528 --> 00:01:12.739
We cannot wage it without
the support of the North.

28
00:01:12.822 --> 00:01:14.467
HARRY COLLETT: Well. it
was all about history.

29
00:01:14.491 --> 00:01:16.743
There were pledges that
were made back in the day.

30
00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:21.414
and Jace is sent to remind
Cregan Stark of those pledges.

31
00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:24.209
If your greybeards can fight.
the Queen will have them.

32
00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:27.712
They will fight hard.
like Northerners.

33
00:01:30.298 --> 00:01:32.801
ALAN TAYLOR: Rhaenyra heard
the news that Luke has died

34
00:01:32.967 --> 00:01:34.277
on a mission that
she sent him on.

35
00:01:34.301 --> 00:01:35.553
so there's guilt involved.

36
00:01:35.637 --> 00:01:38.765
And she's a mother
who's lost a son

37
00:01:38.848 --> 00:01:39.640
and has to go through

38
00:01:39.723 --> 00:01:41.726
the sort of necessary
grieving process

39
00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:43.520
that Daemon. her husband.

40
00:01:43.561 --> 00:01:45.979
can't really appreciate
or understand.

41
00:01:46.231 --> 00:01:49.067
She goes and tries to make
peace with Luke's demise.

42
00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.169
but she cannot settle in it

43
00:01:50.193 --> 00:01:51.473
because it is
unsettled business.

44
00:01:51.527 --> 00:01:53.905
until part of Arrax
washes ashore.

45
00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:57.575
Going in search of evidence is

46
00:01:57.616 --> 00:01:59.327
quite fundamentally
important to her.

47
00:01:59.411 --> 00:02:03.748
I guess one of the sort of
maddest things about death

48
00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.250
is that it seems
sort of impossible.

49
00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:08.836
especially because really the
overriding feeling often is

50
00:02:08.919 --> 00:02:10.213
you just sit with the absence.

51
00:02:10.295 --> 00:02:13.133
And so. anything that has.
like. a tangibility about it

52
00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:14.759
I think is vitally important.

53
00:02:14.843 --> 00:02:18.138
Her son's cloak. the
wing of his dragon.

54
00:02:18.221 --> 00:02:19.723
I think it's devastating.

55
00:02:19.764 --> 00:02:24.102
but I think it galvanizes
a vengeful feeling.

56
00:02:24.436 --> 00:02:27.272
one that maybe she hasn't paid
so much mind to previously.

57
00:02:27.939 --> 00:02:30.150
(SYRAX ROARS)

58
00:02:31.776 --> 00:02:34.213
EVE BEST: I think that Rhaenys
is probably one of the few people

59
00:02:34.237 --> 00:02:35.947
that Daemon knows
he can't mess with.

60
00:02:36.031 --> 00:02:37.906
although I suspect
probably wants to.

61
00:02:39.451 --> 00:02:40.952
We're going to King's Landing.

62
00:02:41.036 --> 00:02:43.038
- To what end?
- Killing Vhagar.

63
00:02:43.413 --> 00:02:45.290
When those two meet.
it's kind of like

64
00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:50.003
a panther meets a
kind of electric eel.

65
00:02:50.086 --> 00:02:52.464
Really dangerous combination.

66
00:02:52.714 --> 00:02:56.134
He's essentially ready to
go to war and get payback.

67
00:02:56.551 --> 00:02:58.237
RYAN CONDAL: It was nice
to throw those characters

68
00:02:58.261 --> 00:02:59.888
into conflict with one another.

69
00:03:00.305 --> 00:03:02.891
I think you can tell
from even her demeanor

70
00:03:02.932 --> 00:03:04.684
the way Rhaenys
thinks of Daemon.

71
00:03:04.809 --> 00:03:06.644
Daemon believes that
he's. of course.

72
00:03:06.728 --> 00:03:07.728
completely in the right

73
00:03:07.771 --> 00:03:09.939
and has the power to
order Rhaenys around.

74
00:03:10.106 --> 00:03:11.316
Fly with me.

75
00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:13.735
It is a command.

76
00:03:13.985 --> 00:03:15.737
Would that you were the king.

77
00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:17.965
AEGON II TARGARYEN:
Where is Jaehaerys?

78
00:03:17.989 --> 00:03:19.324
What do you need of him?

79
00:03:19.616 --> 00:03:21.201
I'm taking him to
the Small Council.

80
00:03:21.785 --> 00:03:24.079
He'll be king one day. He
must begin his instruction.

81
00:03:24.329 --> 00:03:26.373
What if he does not
want to be king?

82
00:03:27.832 --> 00:03:28.832
(WHISPERS) Where is he?

83
00:03:28.958 --> 00:03:30.478
One of the things I loved
about Game of Thrones

84
00:03:30.502 --> 00:03:31.586
was the character humor.

85
00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:33.380
And. you know. we can
spend a lot of time

86
00:03:33.463 --> 00:03:34.506
being dour in this world.

87
00:03:34.589 --> 00:03:36.007
and it's so important
to have humor.

88
00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:37.091
And when I first saw

89
00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:38.694
what Tom Glynn-Carney
was doing with Aegon.

90
00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:40.988
I thought. "He's finding humor
where I didn't know it existed."

91
00:03:41.012 --> 00:03:42.138
And it's painful.

92
00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:43.765
a guy who's way
in over his head.

93
00:03:43.848 --> 00:03:45.183
who really wants to do well

94
00:03:45.266 --> 00:03:47.018
but just can't make
a right move...

95
00:03:47.102 --> 00:03:49.145
(LAUGHS) no matter
what he does.

96
00:03:49.521 --> 00:03:51.690
SPEAKER 2: Aegon
the Magnanimous.

97
00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.441
Hail King Aegon!

98
00:03:54.359 --> 00:03:55.694
The Magnanimous?

99
00:03:57.529 --> 00:03:59.864
I think Aegon is
the kind of father

100
00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:02.742
that encourages bad behavior
because he finds it funny.

101
00:04:02.826 --> 00:04:03.868
He loves his kids.

102
00:04:03.952 --> 00:04:05.370
I have no doubt about that.

103
00:04:05.412 --> 00:04:06.663
He loves his kids dearly.

104
00:04:06.705 --> 00:04:09.290
But he's not one
to discipline them.

105
00:04:09.374 --> 00:04:11.251
If anything. he's. you know.

106
00:04:11.376 --> 00:04:12.687
having competitions
with his children

107
00:04:12.711 --> 00:04:14.879
to see who can be
the most rebellious.

108
00:04:15.213 --> 00:04:16.673
And Aegon often wins.

109
00:04:16.755 --> 00:04:17.755
He took my piece.

110
00:04:17.841 --> 00:04:19.926
Is the heir to the throne
bothering you. Tyland?

111
00:04:20.635 --> 00:04:22.595
We see him come into a
Small Council meeting

112
00:04:22.679 --> 00:04:23.679
with Jaehaerys.

113
00:04:23.722 --> 00:04:26.266
and. you know. he's
spurring him on.

114
00:04:26.391 --> 00:04:29.811
He's wanting him to be more
of a... more of a rebel.

115
00:04:29.894 --> 00:04:32.564
more of a nuisance.
just like his old man.

116
00:04:32.647 --> 00:04:35.233
- I think he wants a ride.
- ALICENT HIGHTOWER: Your Grace.

117
00:04:35.316 --> 00:04:37.110
- TYLAND LANNISTER: A ride?
- A pony ride.

118
00:04:37.819 --> 00:04:39.195
Wouldn't that be fun. Jaehaerys?

119
00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:41.614
Should the Master of
Coin be your royal steed?

120
00:04:41.698 --> 00:04:43.033
(ALL CHUCKLING)

121
00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:44.593
It's meant to be a
moment of fun. a bit.

122
00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:47.746
And yes. like Aegon brings
his four-year-old to work.

123
00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:49.873
But I think on a perhaps
nuanced character level.

124
00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:52.500
this is the thing that
Viserys never did for Aegon.

125
00:04:52.584 --> 00:04:54.437
And Aegon did not study
at the feet of his father.

126
00:04:54.461 --> 00:04:56.838
His father had his male heir
and then essentially said.

127
00:04:56.921 --> 00:04:59.132
"Well. that box is
ticked." He was ill.

128
00:04:59.424 --> 00:05:00.759
I think he enjoyed having a son.

129
00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.053
but didn't put in the work
the way he did with Rhaenyra

130
00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:04.179
when he was a younger man.

131
00:05:04.262 --> 00:05:05.930
And I think Aegon resents that

132
00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:07.557
and feels that
part of the reason

133
00:05:07.599 --> 00:05:09.225
that he's not seen
as being suited

134
00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:11.394
for the crown or the throne

135
00:05:11.603 --> 00:05:14.439
is because he didn't get that
training from his father.

136
00:05:14.564 --> 00:05:17.150
so now he's going to
make up for that tenfold

137
00:05:17.233 --> 00:05:18.443
with Jaehaerys.

138
00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:23.114
ALAN: Alicent's been in a
marriage that was loving.

139
00:05:23.198 --> 00:05:27.118
but not exactly romantic or
physical for quite some time.

140
00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:28.912
Cole has got a lot of issues.

141
00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:30.395
One thing I love
about the character

142
00:05:30.455 --> 00:05:32.165
is that he is a knight
in shining armor

143
00:05:32.248 --> 00:05:33.528
and sort of classically handsome

144
00:05:33.582 --> 00:05:35.710
and probably the most messed
up person in the story

145
00:05:35.794 --> 00:05:36.794
in many ways.

146
00:05:36.878 --> 00:05:38.731
You know. clinging to
notions of purity and duty

147
00:05:38.755 --> 00:05:41.383
and just flagrantly breaking
them left and right.

148
00:05:41.758 --> 00:05:43.118
So. there's a lot
of complex things

149
00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:44.969
driving the moves
closer and closer

150
00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:46.137
between Alicent and Cole.

151
00:05:46.429 --> 00:05:47.639
And it takes a leap forward.

152
00:05:47.681 --> 00:05:48.949
But nothing is simple with them.

153
00:05:48.973 --> 00:05:50.850
so for every leap forward.
there's a push back.

154
00:05:51.142 --> 00:05:53.728
We cannot... again.

155
00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.790
ALAN: There's a lot of
wonderful tension there.

156
00:05:55.814 --> 00:05:58.900
I mean. I think there's love.
but there's a lot of mess too.

157
00:05:58.983 --> 00:05:59.984
(LAUGHS)

158
00:06:00.402 --> 00:06:01.903
- Your Grace.
- Good day.

159
00:06:01.986 --> 00:06:03.405
FABIEN FRANKEL: I
think. ultimately.

160
00:06:03.613 --> 00:06:08.827
they're two very lost people
in a pretty unforgiving world.

161
00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.454
And I think there's always been.

162
00:06:11.496 --> 00:06:13.498
you know. since the
very first episode.

163
00:06:13.623 --> 00:06:15.463
Alicent. you know. had
her eye on Criston Cole.

164
00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:17.419
And then she was a young lady.

165
00:06:17.502 --> 00:06:20.797
and now she's the Queen
of the Seven Kingdoms.

166
00:06:21.339 --> 00:06:23.800
OLIVIA COOKE: It's paramount
that she keeps it a secret

167
00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:27.012
because not only
would her respect

168
00:06:27.095 --> 00:06:29.139
completely disintegrate.

169
00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:31.599
but her stay in the castle.

170
00:06:31.683 --> 00:06:34.352
And Aegon is so unpredictable.
Who knows what he would do

171
00:06:34.436 --> 00:06:38.189
if he found out that his
mother was having sex

172
00:06:38.273 --> 00:06:40.400
with his Commander
of the Kingsguard?

173
00:06:40.525 --> 00:06:42.277
I mean. not only is
it an embarrassment.

174
00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:45.947
it would bring deep. deep shame.

175
00:06:49.534 --> 00:06:52.162
I want Aemond Targaryen.

176
00:06:53.538 --> 00:06:56.249
Rhaenyra has literally one
line in the first episode.

177
00:06:56.374 --> 00:06:57.542
and the one line she says.

178
00:06:57.876 --> 00:07:00.003
Daemon takes as
pulling the trigger.

179
00:07:00.211 --> 00:07:02.881
In our first episode. we
see him unleash something

180
00:07:02.964 --> 00:07:05.383
that is sort of famous in the
lore of House of the Dragon.

181
00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:07.594
a nasty event that he triggers.

182
00:07:08.053 --> 00:07:11.765
When Rhaenyra declares
that she wants Aemond.

183
00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:16.728
I think it's an admission of
a possibly shameful desire.

184
00:07:16.853 --> 00:07:19.856
and I think that admission
is made directly to Daemon.

185
00:07:20.023 --> 00:07:23.026
I think it's also an
admission of their similarity.

186
00:07:23.109 --> 00:07:26.071
She sort of discloses
another way in which

187
00:07:26.154 --> 00:07:28.907
they actually share a darkness.

188
00:07:29.574 --> 00:07:32.409
"I want Aemond Targaryen"
becomes the battle cry

189
00:07:32.494 --> 00:07:34.704
that then resonates
across the entire season

190
00:07:34.788 --> 00:07:37.374
because that is the
next domino to fall

191
00:07:37.457 --> 00:07:40.001
in this back and forth
that sets in motion

192
00:07:40.085 --> 00:07:41.961
a horrible attack
and counterattack

193
00:07:42.045 --> 00:07:43.045
that continues.

194
00:07:43.171 --> 00:07:45.548
and the atrocities grow
worse and worse as they go.

195
00:07:46.049 --> 00:07:47.759
ALAN: In our story.
it's Mysaria.

196
00:07:47.801 --> 00:07:49.945
who has got her tentacles into
every part of King's Landing.

197
00:07:49.969 --> 00:07:52.055
who is able to provide
the connections

198
00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:54.432
for Daemon to exact revenge.

199
00:07:54.516 --> 00:07:56.118
I think it really is a
big deal for the fans

200
00:07:56.142 --> 00:07:57.536
because it keeps
getting referred to.

201
00:07:57.560 --> 00:07:59.521
And I don't know the
characters' actual names.

202
00:07:59.604 --> 00:08:01.773
They're forever in lore
as Blood and Cheese.

203
00:08:01.856 --> 00:08:04.192
- (LAUGHING)
- Who the fuck is she?

204
00:08:04.275 --> 00:08:05.735
She's the Queen. she is.

205
00:08:05.777 --> 00:08:07.696
"A son for a son." he said.

206
00:08:07.779 --> 00:08:09.298
The boldest thing that
I think we did there

207
00:08:09.322 --> 00:08:11.991
was decide to give the last
ten minutes of the episode

208
00:08:12.117 --> 00:08:14.619
over to these two characters
that we have never met before

209
00:08:14.703 --> 00:08:17.455
and rely on them to take us
through the end of the story

210
00:08:17.539 --> 00:08:19.124
and to see. hopefully.

211
00:08:19.165 --> 00:08:21.084
as they go deeper and
deeper into the Red Keep

212
00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:23.062
and as we're spending more
and more screen time on them

213
00:08:23.086 --> 00:08:25.505
that something horrible is
going to happen in there.

214
00:08:25.588 --> 00:08:27.966
and knowing that you're
watching Game of Thrones

215
00:08:28.008 --> 00:08:30.760
and you don't know what is going
to come for you from where.

216
00:08:30.969 --> 00:08:32.886
And seeing that play
out hopefully is the fun

217
00:08:32.971 --> 00:08:35.807
and the horror for the
audience that's yet to come.

218
00:08:36.099 --> 00:08:38.351
♪ (MUSIC SWELLS) ♪

219
00:08:38.476 --> 00:08:39.644
(MUFFLED YELP)

220
00:08:40.687 --> 00:08:42.230
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪
